<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Rim-Gnoblins genes swapped for the equivalents other mods ship, with each retired gene going on this mod's
		Cherry Picker list.
		  - The gnoblin's tox glands become Alpha Genes' venom fangs.
		  - Its extreme dwarfism becomes Big and Small's small frame, and the xenotype also gains small people toughness
		    (BS_TinyTough). Dwarfism only shrinks the body; B&amp;S pairs its small frames with a toughness gene, so this
		    keeps small-frame pawns as durable as B&amp;S intends. Small people toughness requires a small frame, which the
		    swap provides, and has no melee restriction (dwarven grit was rejected because the gnoblin's weak melee damage
		    disables it). It is skipped where the xenotype already has it.
		  - Its rapid development gene becomes a short lifespan gene: relabelled, lifespan factor 0.65 -> 0.5, metabolism
		    -2 -> +2, its childhood growth curve removed, and its aging exclusion tags replaced by a new Lifespan tag.
		    The gnoblin gains VRE - Pigskin's fast aging (2x aging speed for life) to carry the aging side. The two do
		    not exclude each other (fast aging keeps its own Aging tag), so both apply and both count towards metabolism.
		  - Det's Stoneborn long lifespan joins the Lifespan group, so it and short lifespan exclude each other.
		This folder only loads when Rim-Gnoblins is active (see loadFolders.xml); each swap sits in a subfolder gated on the mod that supplies the replacement.
		Operations that also need another mod sit in a subfolder gated on it in loadFolders.xml.

		Verified against the current 1.6 releases: AG_VenomFangs, BS_SmallFrame and VRE_FastAging all exist, and
		DV_LifespanLong has no exclusionTags of its own so that add creates one. The Lifespan group is invented by this
		project rather than defined upstream; its only members (Age_RapidDevelopment and DV_LifespanLong) are both in
		this file, so it is complete.
		Verified 2026-11-07 against Rim-Gnoblins (3018569666, which supports up to 1.6): the Gnoblin xenotype,
		RG_ToxGlands, Size_ExtremeDwarfism and Age_RapidDevelopment all exist, every operation applies in simulation,
		and the folder gate's packageId (VexedTrees980.RimGnoblinsBiotech) is correct. The gnoblin is the only
		installed xenotype with Size_ExtremeDwarfism, and BS_TinyTough shares no exclusion tag with its genes.
		Fix 2026-10-03: a retired gene is now swapped in every xenotype that carries it (not just this mod's), and only
		retired under the same mods as its replacement. Before, other mods' xenotypes sharing the gene (and this one, when
		the replacement mod was absent) lost it to Cherry Picker with nothing in its place.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
		<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="Gnoblin"]/genes/li[text()="RG_ToxGlands"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<li>AG_VenomFangs</li>
		</value>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/CherryPicker.DefList[defName="MMMM_ConvergenceGenetics_CherryPicker_Basics"]/defs</xpath>
		<value>
			<li>GeneDef/RG_ToxGlands</li>
			<li>GeneDef/RG_ToxGlands_Astrogene</li>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
